# The linter CI runs over the playbooks (KAT-648 T-007 Step 7), with the same Ansible
# a person runs. It reads the playbooks: CI runs none of them, reaches no cluster and
# holds no credential (KAT-648 §8 Q10).
#
# Each pin is the newest release at least a week old when it was chosen (ARD-059 §2).
# requirements-lint.lock is generated from this file with every hash, on linux/amd64:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --pip-args "--uploaded-prior-to P7D" \
#     -o requirements-lint.lock requirements-lint.in
-r requirements.in
-c requirements.lock
ansible-lint==26.10.1
